     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. You confirmed it yourself, but I asked for confirmation from your supervising physician. A medical student's confirmation doesn't cover that. The dose is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum. At that level the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, outweighs any benefit I can see.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin.\n- **Hold off until your attending or resident reviews it.** If they decide on a dose above the labeled maximum, they should enter it themselves or tell you the rationale. I'd expect that to be rare.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you'd like, I'll enter it right away."
